            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0299" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6131/305: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-04-02T17:00:00+03:00">April 2, 1935—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 2—6:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>133. Your 71, March 27, 9 p.m. Saw Litvinov this afternoon. He stated that he
                    would confer with Rosengoltz and give me written reply. He attempted to assume
                    that “vague” assurances would suffice. I insisted that you would expect a
                    definite commitment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
